Here's a real countdown to a fixed end time. It's just as effective when the sale actually ends:

```html
<div id="sale">Sale ends in <span id="t"></span></div>
<script>
  const end = new Date('2026-10-01T23:59:00-04:00');
  function tick() {
    const ms = end - new Date();
    if (ms <= 0) { document.getElementById('sale').textContent = 'Sale has ended'; return; }
    const h = Math.floor(ms / 3.6e6), m = Math.floor(ms % 3.6e6 / 6e4), s = Math.floor(ms % 6e4 / 1000);
